/-!
# Realization of integral pullback comparisons

We show that the integral pullback and scalar-extension comparisons can be realized by a single
strict comparison system satisfying all coherence laws.

## Implementation details

The sequence site retains the whole quotient diagram. Its pullback is the left adjoint of the
sectionwise direct image. Scalar change is the universal derived change of rings for the map of
quotient coefficient sheaves.

The comparisons are built on strict towers: a flat-term K-flat representative of `K` is reduced
termwise to quotient towers, and the strict-tower homotopy limit (via K-injective tower
resolutions) realizes these as total derived inverse limits. The composition, scalar-association
and unit comparisons are the canonical finite-level maps, so all coherence equations hold as
strict-system equations and are transported by `Rlim`; independence of the choices follows from
the uniqueness of comparisons between resolutions. Rationalization sends equal strict tower maps
to equal maps, with no finite Tor-amplitude assumption.

## References

* [Stacks, Tag 099N], [Stacks, Tag 0D6D], [Stacks, Tag 06YY], [Stacks, Tag 0941]
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false
set_option synthInstance.maxSize 4096
attribute [-instance] CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_of_essentiallySmall
attribute [-instance] WeilConjectures.sfAbSheafify WeilConjectures.sfAbBijective

universe t u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
namespace WeilConjectures
open scoped ChangeOfRings

variable (l : ℕ) [Fact l.Prime] (E : Type u) [Field E]
  [Algebra ℚ_[l] E] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[l] E]
  (L : Type u) [Field L] [Algebra ℚ_[l] L] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[l] L]
  (ι : E →ₐ[ℚ_[l]] L)

/-- There is an integral comparison system whose pullback and scalar-extension comparisons for
`ι : E →ₐ[ℚ_[l]] L` are realized on strict systems, with the normalized counits, finite
reductions and all coherence laws. -/
theorem integralPullbackComparisonRealization
    (l : ℕ) [Fact l.Prime] (E : Type u) [Field E]
    [Algebra ℚ_[l] E] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[l] E]
    (L : Type u) [Field L] [Algebra ℚ_[l] L]
    [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[l] L] (ι : E →ₐ[ℚ_[l]] L) :
    ∃ D : IntegralComparisonSystem l,
      IntegralComparisonRealizationCoherence l E L ι D := by
  obtain ⟨D, hD⟩ := integralPullbackComparisonRealization_simultaneous.{u} l
  exact ⟨D, hD E L ι⟩

end WeilConjectures
